                <pb facs="1089" n="979" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg979"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.801 Search/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Adams</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-23T16:00:00+08:00">December 23, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 23—7:12 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. My 125, December 12, 1 p.m. No representations have been made by the Chinese
                    authorities and I am inclined to believe that none will be made since the troops
                    who were put off the <hi rendition="#italic">Ifung</hi> have left this area.</p>
                <p>Legation and Nanking informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adams</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
